 "relevance_note": "Review whose text gives individual-level features for two previously published HA20/TNFAIP3 patients, e.g. \"A patient with ALPS presented with fevers, bilateral cervical lymphadenopathy, extensive skin rash, and massive hepatosplenomegaly.\"",
 "method_note": "Review (Aksentijevich & Zhou 2017). Rows built with a small Python script from my own reading; Table 2 cells for the ref (35) column were located by script and checked by eye against the table. Two in-scope people: (1) 'ref (16) patient' = the one patient among Zhou et al.'s 11 (ref 16) described as initially diagnosed with SLE with CNS vasculitis and ITP; the sentence prints no reference itself, the label uses the preceding citation (16). (2) 'ref (35) patient' = the Japanese ALPS patient (text cites (35)); Table 2 has a single-patient column 'Patients (35) (n = 1)', whose 1/1 cells were recorded as observed for this person (column header quoted as a second span). Its 0/1 cells were NOT recorded as excluded, following the zero-count rule literally even though n = 1; '/' cells are not reported per the legend. Variant for ref (35) patient: Figure 2 legend gives 'the reported p.Gln415fs (35)' and the four-nucleotide deletion 'reported as c.1245_1248del'; the review's authors propose the corrected names c.1249_1252del and p.Lys417Serfs*4 for the same mutation (not recorded as a separate variant row). The attribution of c.1245_1248del to ref 35 is by adjacency in the legend. Pathogenicity 'novel LOF' comes from a statement about the named group (two Japanese families and the ALPS patient, refs 35-37). Ref (16) patient has a TNFAIP3 variant row with 'not reported' because the variants of Zhou et al. appear only in Figure 2. Group-level only, no rows: Zhou et al.'s other 10 patients (ref 16, n = 11), Patients (37) (n = 6) and Patients (36) (n = 3), the two Japanese entero-BD families, and all otulipenia/LUBAC patients (other genes). Table 2 HA20 columns hold group counts only. 'Fevers' for ref (35) patient was not mapped to checklist 'recurrent fever' (recurrence not stated). Normal CD3+CD8+ subpopulations recorded as an excluded abnormality (D-27). n_patients_reported and cohort_size_as_stated left null: no total stated. Possible internal inconsistency: Table 2 'Elevated CRP, ESR' gives 6/6 for ref 16 (n = 11) and 1/1 for ref 37 (n = 6), so denominators differ from the column headers; not used for any person except the n = 1 column. No stacked ' / ' cells in this paper.",
